  Docs\LEVEL1.md:87:
  Docs\LEVEL1.md:88:## Later levels (proposed; decided after Level 1 plays well)
  Docs\LEVEL1.md:89:
  Docs\LEVEL1.md:90:1. Level 2: orders reach a crew at its next shift unless Site is standing there, and Site gets a 
Stop button.
  Docs\LEVEL1.md:91:2. Level 3: permits and the open-trench limit, with Rules holding the cards.
  Docs\LEVEL1.md:92:3. Level 4: rain, the forecast and the pump.
  Docs\LEVEL1.md:93:4. Then inspections at zone ends, field mistakes (an order that never arrived), money, and the 
Stage 3 cities. The full design stays in `Docs/DESIGN_v0.md`.
> Docs\DECISIONS.md:45:| K37 | The warp is a materialization, never a mask: the site is drawn where a wave from the 
player's feet has passed (wire and blueprint lines first, then surfaces), the room shows wherever the site is not yet 
drawn, and nothing covers the view; the sky closes last | Bryan, October 21, third headset test: the sphere mask read 
as a fisheye lens and stuck as a window | `LEVEL1.md`, `XR_RENDERING.md`, WO-L5 |
> Docs\DECISIONS.md:46:| K38 | The site must read as a real site: textured ground with relief, real trench geometry 
with spoil and pipe, props, a sky with sun and clouds, shadows and haze, within the Quest 3S budget; every site 
material on one shader so site-wide effects apply at once | Bryan, October 21: the assets were extremely poor, a 
horizontal line like a drawing | WO-L4, `XR_RENDERING.md` |
> Docs\DECISIONS.md:47:| K39 | The Plan page is the site office: a drafting board inked day by day, a radio console 
with switches, the PM with a face and a bubble, a calendar, synthesized sound; the information rules do not change | 
Bryan, October 21: the page worked but did not feel like a game | WO-L3 |
> Docs\DECISIONS.md:48:| K40 | Passthrough rules are fixed in `Docs/XR_RENDERING.md` (alpha-0 clear, HDR and 
post-processing off, dome sky, premultiplied alpha, no full-view meshes, foveation Low, render scale 1.0) and every 
headset work order lists it under Read | Two builds failed on compositing | `XR_RENDERING.md`, 
`.claude/skills/quest-mr-rendering/` |
  Docs\DECISIONS.md:49:| K41 | The orchestrator does not build for the Quest; it verifies in the Editor (tests, 
screenshots, alpha composites for passthrough states, stats) and stops with the build steps; Bryan builds with Build 
and Run Quest and judges in the headset | Bryan, October 21: do not spend tokens on builds | 
`ORCHESTRATOR_SHOWCASE.md` Round 5 |
